<title>SPAIN: Bankinter nine-month pre-tax profit rises 14 pct.</title>
<headline>Bankinter nine-month pre-tax profit rises 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for first nine months in billions of pesetas, unless stated:</p>
<p> Pretax profit			   19.228   vs   16.837</p>
<p> Net taxed				 13.137   vs   11.521</p>
<p> Cash flow				 40.008   vs   26.526</p>
<p> Total assets			 1,753.397   vs   1,296.055</p>
<p> Operating costs			 19.692   vs   18.296</p>
<p> Operating margin			23.601   vs   17.731</p>
<p> Extraordinary results		 -1.255   vs   -0.579</p>
<p>NOTE - Bankinter said client business rose 15.8 percent to 16.4 billion pesetas in the first nine months of the year while in the capital markets area profit was 6.4 billion pesetas, up 238 percent on the same period last year.</p>
<p>The percentage of doubtful debts against credit investment and risks of the firm was 1.12 percent, one of the lowest in the sector, it added.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
